# Cursor Rules for PAKH_PRECHECK
# Refer to AGENTS.md for full architecture map

# 1. TOKEN EFFICIENCY & SPEED RULES:
- NEVER create temporary scratch/test scripts in scratch/ or run one-off find functions.
- ALWAYS use fast indexed ripgrep/grep to find symbols and exact line locations in milliseconds.
- ALWAYS use precision chunk edits (diff-based) instead of rewriting entire files.
- NEVER execute live OneOSS ticket submissions without explicit user confirmation.
- STRICTLY FORBIDDEN: NEVER add random/unnecessary emojis or icons (🤖, ⚡, 🚀, 🎉, ⭐, etc.) to the WebApp UI (buttons, labels, select options, alerts). Keep the interface strictly professional, clean, and enterprise-grade.

# 2. KEY REPOSITORY MAP:
- Service IDs & Throttling: serviceid.json
- Scenarios Engine (Data/Radio/Core): scenarios_engine.py & diagnostic_scenarios.json
- Reporting & Closing Bot: report_bot.py
- Ticket API & Precheck Orchestration: routers/tickets.py
- Web SPA & Routes: routers/web.py, templates/dashboard.html
- Database: db_manager.py, tickets.db
- Integrations: ttsnew_api.py, tts_old_api.py, btools_manager.py, sapccheck/, cem_client.py
